  "body": "> I am not sure where else to ask/discuss this, so I try it here. Feel free to point me to the right place and close it here.\r\n\r\nI have developed my first PWA using the Web Serial API. Right now I am telling users: use an up to date version of Chrome or Edge, but obviously they keep asking: What's with mobile? What's with $BROWSER_X?\r\n\r\nSo I was wondering, are there any plans of the Web Serial API to be implemented on Chrome for Android for example? I was not able to find anything to that regard - probably I am looking in the wrong place.\r\n\r\nAlso Mozilla and Safari sent strong signals against implementing this feature - I was wondering if enough user pressure might persuade them into implementing it anyway - are there any cases in which those vendors took a strong stance against something and then still went ahead implementing it?",
